$\mathrm{Ag}^{+}+\mathrm{Br}^{-} \rightleftharpoons \mathrm{AgBr}$ Precipitation starts when ionic product just exceeds solubility product

$\begin{aligned} \mathrm{K}_{\text{sp }}= \left[\mathrm{Ag}^{+}\right]\left[\mathrm{Br}^{-}\right]\\
& {\left[\mathrm{Br}^{-}\right]=\frac{\mathrm{K}_{\mathrm{sp}}}{\left[\mathrm{Ag}^{+}\right]}=\frac{5 \times 10^{-13}}{0.05}=10^{-11}}
\end{aligned}

i.e., precipitation just starts when 10^{-11}$ moles of $\mathrm{KBr}  is added to 1 \mathrm{ L} of  \mathrm{AgNO}_3 solution.
No. of moles of \mathrm{KBr} to $be added

\begin{aligned}
\therefore$\text{ weight$ of } $\mathrm{KBr} \text{ to be added } & =10^{-11} \times120 \\
& =1.2 \times10^{-9}  \mathrm{ g}$
\end{aligned}

